Third-party notices for Arkime (https://arkime.com), Apache-2.0.

This file is generated at build time by release/notice.txt.pl and has four
parts, in this order:

  1. Code built into capture: libraries statically linked on platforms whose
     OS does not package them, and the C sources compiled in.
  2. Files shipped as-is with viewer: the scripts in viewer/public and CyberChef.
  3. npm packages installed for the Node.js servers (viewer, cont3xt,
     parliament, wise), from the production dependency trees.
  4. npm packages vite inlined into the browser bundles of the four Vue apps.

Arkime capture also links against libraries provided by the operating system.
They are declared as package dependencies and are not distributed with Arkime,
so their licenses ship with the operating system and are not repeated here:

  glib2 (LGPL-2.1), libcurl (curl), libpcap (BSD), libmaxminddb (Apache-2.0),
  nghttp2 (MIT), libyaml (MIT), libmagic (BSD), zlib (zlib), zstd (BSD),
  lua (MIT), OpenSSL (Apache-2.0), libxdp (LGPL-2.1 or BSD-2-Clause), and on
  Linux distributions that package them, yara (BSD-3-Clause) and librdkafka
  (BSD-2-Clause). The optional pfring plugin dynamically links libpfring
  (LGPL-2.1).

The bundled Node.js runtime is MIT, see https://github.com/nodejs/node.

